On every hill looking down on their cave,

269
00:21:57,760 --> 00:22:00,399
...there are good nokers.

270
00:22:01,280 --> 00:22:04,639
They must have blocked the valley completely.

271
00:22:06,120 --> 00:22:12,079
In case of an attack, they let
each other know with red arrows.

272
00:22:13,760 --> 00:22:17,199
It'll be very hard to get inside.

273
00:22:17,760 --> 00:22:20,199
Dogs.

274
00:22:20,560 --> 00:22:23,199
They're laying traps all around.

275
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:26,079
My Shahzade.

276
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:30,559
Their cave is well protected.

277
00:22:31,040 --> 00:22:32,679
Yes.

278
00:22:34,480 --> 00:22:35,879
First,

279
00:22:39,520 --> 00:22:41,959
...we need to kill the archers on the hills.

280
00:22:42,040 --> 00:22:43,439
We are just a few.

281
00:22:43,840 --> 00:22:45,839
If they manage to send a message,

282
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:48,079
...we will fail.

283
00:22:48,880 --> 00:22:52,599
Orhan Bey is right.

284
00:22:52,960 --> 00:22:54,719
Before they die,

285
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:58,159
..they will shoot the red arrows.

286
00:22:59,600 --> 00:23:03,439
Well... So..

287
00:23:05,800 --> 00:23:08,159
How will we get inside?

288
00:23:08,640 --> 00:23:11,639
My Shahzade, we can attack through the valley.

289
00:23:11,920 --> 00:23:13,719
We can hit them from their back.

290
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:17,079
We’ll arrive there in time
and save Elcim Hatun’s family.

291
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:19,639
Those dogs only speak this language.

292
00:23:19,800 --> 00:23:22,879
-We should attack.
-No.

293
00:23:24,160 --> 00:23:27,039
They will kill your family instantly.

294
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:33,999
-Aykurt.
-My Shahzade.

295
00:23:34,520 --> 00:23:36,119
Tell the bey of the tribe...

296
00:23:36,240 --> 00:23:39,079
...to give me his best ten alps.

297
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:42,959
Being too many is useless.

298
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:45,399
Orhan Bey.

299
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:48,639
What’s your plan?

300
00:23:48,800 --> 00:23:51,079
How will we get in their cave?

301
00:23:56,840 --> 00:24:00,319
By using our most effective weapon.

302
00:24:02,080 --> 00:24:04,199
We’ll leave at dawn. Come on!

303
00:24:04,280 --> 00:24:07,039
As you order, my Shahzadej

304
00:24:15,840 --> 00:24:17,679
Let me help you, father.

305
00:24:17,800 --> 00:24:19,839
I don't want!

306
00:24:22,320 --> 00:24:24,879
I don’t want.

307
00:24:25,320 --> 00:24:28,719
I don’t want anything from you anymore.

308
00:24:31,600 --> 00:24:33,399
Yakup Bey.

309
00:24:33,600 --> 00:24:37,119
I did this to...

310
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:40,559
Don’t you even speak.

311
00:24:45,760 --> 00:24:47,919
Mehmed is young...

312
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:50,319
...and inexperienced.

313
00:24:50,760 --> 00:24:53,679
He made a mistake.

314
00:24:57,080 --> 00:24:59,079
But you

315
00:24:59,360 --> 00:25:01,759
Who are you...

316
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:06,439
...to try to make my daughter a spy

317
00:25:13,600 --> 00:25:15,839
I'm her mother.

318
00:25:16,240 --> 00:25:19,479
And your hatun, Yakup Bey.

319
00:25:20,080 --> 00:25:22,559
I did this because I cared about our future.

320
00:25:22,640 --> 00:25:26,279
-By using my daughter?
-Yakup Bey.

321
00:25:31,160 --> 00:25:34,679
Say no more.

322
00:25:37,720 --> 00:25:39,839
You made me..

323
00:25:39,960 --> 00:25:42,759
...get my head down, Saadet.

324
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:46,159
Now go...

325
00:25:46,400 --> 00:25:49,359
...and apologize to the hatuns.

326
00:25:49,480 --> 00:25:51,199
What?

327
00:25:55,240 --> 00:25:57,999
You can ask me to do anything.

328
00:25:58,200 --> 00:25:59,919
But not this.

329
00:26:00,040 --> 00:26:03,159
If you want me to forgive you,

330
00:26:03,520 --> 00:26:05,879
...you’ll first ask forgiveness...

331
00:26:06,240 --> 00:26:08,199
...for what you did.

332
00:26:24,280 --> 00:26:26,839
Easy, father.

333
00:26:31,080 --> 00:26:33,199
And you?

334
00:26:33,800 --> 00:26:35,919
How could you...

335
00:26:36,040 --> 00:26:38,879
..do this to me and yourself?

336
00:26:39,640 --> 00:26:42,239
Didn't you think about it at all?

337
00:26:48,920 --> 00:26:52,039
I had nothing else to do, father.

338
00:26:53,680 --> 00:26:57,519
My mother put me in such a tight spot...

339
00:27:19,680 --> 00:27:21,279
When...

340
00:27:21,560 --> 00:27:24,199
...a man loves someone.

341
00:27:24,480 --> 00:27:27,119
...he wants to trust, Gonca.

342
00:27:30,520 --> 00:27:32,439
Today...

343
00:27:32,960 --> 00:27:36,239
...I lost my trust in your mother.

344
00:27:40,760 --> 00:27:43,639
My heart is burning.

345
00:27:46,600 --> 00:27:48,799
Beside this suffering,

346
00:27:49,760 --> 00:27:52,799
...I don't feel this arrow's pain at all.

347
00:28:01,560 --> 00:28:04,479
It's you who started the fire, father.

348
00:28:06,040 --> 00:28:09,039
Now you're blaming my mother, but...

349
00:28:09,720 --> 00:28:13,159
...it was you who first
sent my mother after Kayi.

350
00:28:24,240 --> 00:28:28,159
You are guilty as much as...

351
00:28:31,120 --> 00:28:34,359
....my mother and brother are.

352
00:29:06,480 --> 00:29:09,839
Lords are in our hands now.

353
00:29:11,520 --> 00:29:13,679
Call the Beys now.

354
00:29:13,760 --> 00:29:15,239
Yes my Bey.

355
00:29:37,040 --> 00:29:39,279
Can I tell you something, Bala Hatun?

356
00:29:39,280 --> 00:29:41,039
Saadet Hatun wants to see you.

357
00:29:41,160 --> 00:29:43,199
Aameen.

358
00:29:43,960 --> 00:29:45,879
Let her come, Kismet.

359
00:30:09,480 --> 00:30:12,919
Yes, Saadet Hatun.

360
00:30:17,960 --> 00:30:20,599
I am listening to you.

361
00:30:22,160 --> 00:30:27,279
Yakup Bey regained his health, thanks to Allah.

362
00:30:28,920 --> 00:30:31,399
Thanks to Allah.

363
00:30:32,880 --> 00:30:35,159
Thanks to you...

364
00:30:35,480 --> 00:30:37,959
Thanks to Alaeddin Bey.

365
00:30:41,040 --> 00:30:43,799
I came here to thank you.

366
00:30:43,960 --> 00:30:46,599
We did our duty, Saadet Hatun.

367
00:30:46,760 --> 00:30:50,439
They say ’’everyone does what suits them”.

368
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:53,959
I am expecting you to understand me, Bala.

369
00:30:54,080 --> 00:30:55,959
When I saw my Bey...

370
00:30:56,280 --> 00:30:59,119
...on his deathbed...

371
00:30:59,440 --> 00:31:01,639
..I lost my mind.

372
00:31:01,680 --> 00:31:04,279
I am sorry.

373
00:31:04,760 --> 00:31:07,159
Did you just...

374
00:31:07,600 --> 00:31:10,359
...lose your mind, Saadet Hatun?

375
00:31:13,400 --> 00:31:17,759
How can someone turn her own daughter into a spy?

376
00:31:18,000 --> 00:31:19,719
What kind of a mother are you?

377
00:31:19,760 --> 00:31:21,719
I did not mean to hearm you.

378
00:31:22,120 --> 00:31:24,359
It was misunderstood.

379
00:31:27,280 --> 00:31:29,999
One cannot play with love, Bala.

380
00:31:30,120 --> 00:31:32,439
They fell in love before...

381
00:31:32,640 --> 00:31:35,919
...I gave her the duty.

382
00:31:36,200 --> 00:31:37,919
You..

383
00:31:38,440 --> 00:31:42,519
...you dirtied the love of those two children.

384
00:31:46,720 --> 00:31:50,159
What is done is done.

385
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:53,919
I am paying the price of what I did.

386
00:31:56,400 --> 00:31:58,759
And may you..

387
00:32:04,560 --> 00:32:08,759
...give me your blessings in doomsday.

388
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:19,999
I will not shake that hand, Saadet.

389
00:32:20,640 --> 00:32:22,759
If I really...

390
00:32:22,800 --> 00:32:25,119
...believe that you regret one day...

391
00:32:25,280 --> 00:32:28,079
..then I can shake your hand.

392
00:32:36,360 --> 00:32:39,759
Think well...

393
00:32:39,800 --> 00:32:42,679
..before you do something now.

394
00:32:57,760 --> 00:33:00,559
You won't change, Saadet.

395
00:33:00,760 --> 00:33:03,159
The love you have for power overtook you.

396
00:33:03,360 --> 00:33:06,279
May Allah help you.

397
00:33:09,840 --> 00:33:12,319
Our spies sent us a letter.

398
00:33:12,480 --> 00:33:16,399
Olivia Hatun invited Lords to Atranos.

399
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:19,079
We got rid of the Gorklu Khan issue.

400
00:33:19,560 --> 00:33:22,759
They will take their heads
out of their hiding holes.

401
00:33:23,040 --> 00:33:25,799
They must be after a treacherous move, my Bey.

402
00:33:26,120 --> 00:33:29,359
That is right. Yakup Bey was shot.

403
00:33:29,560 --> 00:33:31,119
Gorklu Khan died.

404
00:33:31,360 --> 00:33:35,359
Now... they will look for
an opportunity to revolt.

405
00:33:35,440 --> 00:33:39,479
-But we won't let them.
-What are we going to do then, my Bey?

406
00:33:39,880 --> 00:33:42,759
We will speak their language.

407
00:33:42,800 --> 00:33:45,799
Konur! Tell our Alps to get ready.

408
00:33:45,960 --> 00:33:49,159
You will surround Atranos when Lords gather.

409
00:33:49,320 --> 00:33:51,159
Yes my Bey.

410
00:33:51,880 --> 00:33:56,679
And we will take the Lord of Kite.

411
00:34:04,840 --> 00:34:06,879
Did you do what my father said, mother?

412
00:34:07,080 --> 00:34:11,239
Yakup

413
00:34:11,320 --> 00:34:15,518
If it wasn't for you, I would destroy this palace!

414
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:17,319
What happened, mother?

415
00:34:17,440 --> 00:34:19,438
That Bala disgraced me!

416
00:34:19,679 --> 00:34:21,438
Disgraced me!

417
00:34:21,600 --> 00:34:23,559
She did not shake my hand!

418
00:34:23,600 --> 00:34:25,998
She made me beg like a dog, Mehmet!

419
00:34:26,360 --> 00:34:29,759
Ah... Ah, my father, ahh!

420
00:34:30,040 --> 00:34:33,799
My father is making a mistake, mother! A mistake!

421
00:34:34,080 --> 00:34:37,638
Will we forgive them
because they saved our lives?

422
00:34:37,880 --> 00:34:40,599
Order me... Order me...

423
00:34:40,639 --> 00:34:41,719
...to burn this palace!

424
00:34:41,840 --> 00:34:44,559
We won't do that, Mehmet.

425
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:46,918
We will core it.

426
00:34:47,159 --> 00:34:49,239
We will core it in such a way that...

427
00:34:49,280 --> 00:34:53,599
...this palace will collapse on them.

428
00:34:54,040 --> 00:34:58,759
They disgraced your father, your
sister and your family before everyone!

429
00:34:58,920 --> 00:35:00,639
They will pay for this.

430
00:35:00,640 --> 00:35:05,279
-We will not stop, Mehmet!
-As you say, mother.

431
00:35:05,640 --> 00:35:09,119
They were our rivals until now.

432
00:35:09,280 --> 00:35:11,799
But after what happened..

433
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:15,519
We have our enemies, Mehmet.

434
00:35:16,880 --> 00:35:18,519
Until now..

435
00:35:18,640 --> 00:35:21,559
..I wanted to hurt their feelings.

436
00:35:21,720 --> 00:35:25,879
But now... I will cut their hearts into pieces.

437
00:35:26,240 --> 00:35:29,039
We will, my mother! We will!

438
00:35:29,400 --> 00:35:33,719
But... don't do something in front of others...

439
00:35:33,800 --> 00:35:36,039
...and make your father angry with you.

440
00:35:36,280 --> 00:35:40,199
We will do it secretly.

441
00:35:40,680 --> 00:35:44,159
We will, mother. We will, don't worry.

442
00:35:58,440 --> 00:36:00,239
Stop!

443
00:36:01,400 --> 00:36:04,119
Stop, where are you going?

444
00:36:04,600 --> 00:36:06,719
Where are you going?

445
00:36:57,360 --> 00:36:59,319
Come.

446
00:36:59,520 --> 00:37:01,639
Where?

447
00:37:02,920 --> 00:37:05,599
Come.

448
00:37:21,720 --> 00:37:25,319
Come..

449
00:37:40,920 --> 00:37:43,519
Where are you going?

450
00:37:50,960 --> 00:37:54,079
The Righteous!

451
00:38:06,040 --> 00:38:09,199
Malhun!

452
00:38:09,640 --> 00:38:11,519
Malhun!

453
00:38:14,280 --> 00:38:18,799
-Osman!
-Don’t be afraid..

454
00:38:19,720 --> 00:38:20,879
My Osman...

455
00:38:21,800 --> 00:38:24,519
Did you have the same dream again?

456
00:38:24,760 --> 00:38:27,919
It was... It was the same.

457
00:38:28,000 --> 00:38:29,999
But...

458
00:38:30,520 --> 00:38:33,079
...you know, I told you that there was a Hatun.

459
00:38:33,120 --> 00:38:37,399
I told you that she was walking towards
a tree but that I couldn't see her face.

460
00:38:37,440 --> 00:38:40,119
Right, you couldn't...

461
00:38:40,560 --> 00:38:42,919
I saw her.

462
00:38:44,800 --> 00:38:46,399
I saw her.

463
00:38:47,440 --> 00:38:50,719
This time, I saw her face.

464
00:38:52,280 --> 00:38:54,999
It was met

465
00:38:56,640 --> 00:38:58,759
I saw myself...

466
00:38:58,800 --> 00:39:01,759
...wearing an ihram.

467
00:39:10,640 --> 00:39:13,119
Malhun...

468
00:39:13,960 --> 00:39:15,119
Look...

469
00:39:16,480 --> 00:39:18,799
I know very well what is in your mind...

470
00:39:18,880 --> 00:39:21,439
...and what is in your heart.

471
00:39:21,520 --> 00:39:23,799
Osman.

472
00:39:24,320 --> 00:39:27,439
What I saw was the way of pilgrimage.

473
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:30,199
But... right before I woke up...

474
00:39:30,200 --> 00:39:32,719
...the horsemen were coming at me again.

475
00:39:32,880 --> 00:39:36,399
I drew my bow and was
about to shoot it when it broke.

476
00:39:37,480 --> 00:39:42,159
Was this a sign?

477
00:39:43,440 --> 00:39:46,719
Is it better to go or to stay?

478
00:39:46,960 --> 00:39:49,919
I am confused.

479
00:39:56,200 --> 00:40:00,239
Now... as you know...

480
00:40:01,000 --> 00:40:03,039
...things are harder now.

481
00:40:03,040 --> 00:40:05,479
We are between two fires.

482
00:40:06,000 --> 00:40:08,719
In the palace, in Yenisehir...

483
00:40:08,760 --> 00:40:11,639
...before the folk, of course...

484
00:40:12,040 --> 00:40:16,279
...of course, your presence here gives me power.

485
00:40:16,440 --> 00:40:19,159
Of course you give me power.

486
00:40:20,560 --> 00:40:23,279
But this dream you had..

487
00:40:24,800 --> 00:40:27,359
...going to Hajj...

488
00:40:35,040 --> 00:40:39,399
Is it better for you to stay or to go?

489
00:40:44,880 --> 00:40:48,199
You have to make that decision.

490
00:40:49,560 --> 00:40:52,439
Look... No matter what happens...

491
00:40:52,520 --> 00:40:55,039
No matter what you decide...

492
00:40:55,440 --> 00:40:58,599
...I will accept it.

493
00:40:59,000 --> 00:41:01,839
I am with you.

494
00:41:02,000 --> 00:41:05,639
May my Allah keep you with us.

495
00:41:25,200 --> 00:41:26,999
Elcim Hatun!

496
00:41:29,680 --> 00:41:34,159
How did Tajeddin Noyan start attacking you?

497
00:41:44,560 --> 00:41:48,839
He asked for an army from
my father for the Mongol war.

498
00:41:50,040 --> 00:41:52,559
And my father rejected him.

499
00:41:56,040 --> 00:41:59,399
When he understood that he was
not going to let us live in peace...

500
00:41:59,720 --> 00:42:02,719
...and that he was going to shed blood...

501
00:42:04,520 --> 00:42:07,759
...we migrated from our lands.

502
00:42:11,760 --> 00:42:14,039
Butthat Tajeddin Noyan..

503
00:42:14,320 --> 00:42:18,399
...is such a bad and revengeful man that...

504
00:42:18,880 --> 00:42:21,119
..he came after us.

505
00:42:21,160 --> 00:42:25,239
He wanted to take his revenge
because we rejected him.

506
00:42:25,840 --> 00:42:30,479
He martyred my mother and my brother.

507
00:42:32,800 --> 00:42:35,479
And he captured us.

508
00:42:38,920 --> 00:42:41,279
Elcim Hatun..

509
00:42:42,360 --> 00:42:45,439
Do you know something important...

510
00:42:45,600 --> 00:42:49,359
...about Tajeddin Noyan’s army?

511
00:42:53,280 --> 00:42:56,999
The assassins I told Osman Bey about.

512
00:42:58,560 --> 00:43:01,639
There is one among them that..

513
00:43:01,960 --> 00:43:04,599
...is the most cruel.

514
00:43:05,560 --> 00:43:09,759
That person was a student of those
who followed the path of Hasan Sabbah.

515
00:43:10,200 --> 00:43:13,799
Maybe that cruel person was
the one who shot Yakup Bey.

516
00:43:15,040 --> 00:43:17,479
Elcim Hatun.

517
00:43:18,600 --> 00:43:21,479
Can we find that cruel person?

518
00:43:23,760 --> 00:43:28,079
No one saw that person
or hear that person's voice.

519
00:43:28,600 --> 00:43:31,559
They say that person takes lives like a shadow...

520
00:43:31,680 --> 00:43:34,439
...and then disappears.

521
00:43:36,480 --> 00:43:39,999
Like a shadow, huh?

522
00:43:40,720 --> 00:43:44,519
We know how to drown that shadow in our light.

523
00:43:44,960 --> 00:43:48,159
We will send them all away
from this land, Elcim Hatun.

524
00:43:48,320 --> 00:43:51,239
All.

525
00:44:09,200 --> 00:44:11,519
Orhan Bey...

526
00:44:12,920 --> 00:44:15,199
Thank you.

527
00:44:15,440 --> 00:44:17,759
For everything.

528
00:44:19,520 --> 00:44:24,159
You are risking your lives
for my father and my aunt.

529
00:44:24,600 --> 00:44:28,359
But you should know...
We do not forget the good...

530
00:44:28,440 --> 00:44:31,359
...or the bad done to us.

531
00:44:31,480 --> 00:44:34,479
We will pay you back for this.

532
00:44:34,760 --> 00:44:37,159
Thank you Elcim Hatun.

533
00:44:37,360 --> 00:44:39,559
But don't worry...

534
00:44:39,640 --> 00:44:41,919
We will take your revenge today...

535
00:44:42,000 --> 00:44:45,439
...and with Allah’s consent, we
will take your father and your aunt.

536
00:44:46,840 --> 00:44:49,199
Come on.

537
00:45:23,040 --> 00:45:24,919
Alaeddin... -How?

538
00:45:25,000 --> 00:45:27,559
Did you have a good time?

539
00:45:29,960 --> 00:45:31,679
What do you mean?

540
00:45:35,520 --> 00:45:39,599
My heart ached every time I saw you.

541
00:45:39,840 --> 00:45:43,799
My conscience took control of my heart, Alaeddin.

542
00:45:46,160 --> 00:45:49,039
I didn’t do any of this on purpose.

543
00:45:49,120 --> 00:45:51,599
-I had to.
-What did you have to do?

544
00:45:51,600 --> 00:45:53,199
What did you have to do?

545
00:45:53,320 --> 00:45:56,159
So that you want to talk, let’s talk.

546
00:45:56,520 --> 00:45:59,999
What did you think? Did
you say ”1 can fool Alaeddin"?

547
00:46:00,040 --> 00:46:03,759
Look, Gonca. I've been thinking
about this since I heard about it.

548
00:46:03,800 --> 00:46:06,599
I've been thinking about
the things we did together.

549
00:46:06,600 --> 00:46:09,239
Which one was real?
Which one was the game?

550
00:46:09,360 --> 00:46:12,159
Tell me; Was your love a game?

551
00:46:12,520 --> 00:46:15,799
Did you play a game when
you risked your life for my life?

552
00:46:15,880 --> 00:46:19,039
If all that was a game..

553
00:46:21,080 --> 00:46:24,719
..how can you still look into my eyes like this?

554
00:46:24,840 --> 00:46:29,559
None of them; I swear, none
of them was a game, Alaeddint

555
00:46:29,840 --> 00:46:33,639
You can say anything to me,
you can do anything to me...

556
00:46:34,040 --> 00:46:38,239
But you cannot put me and
my mother in the same pot.

557
00:46:41,360 --> 00:46:43,679
For me...

558
00:46:43,800 --> 00:46:46,359
...the only thing that is true is you.

559
00:46:46,400 --> 00:46:49,519
My love for you... -No.

560
00:46:50,480 --> 00:46:53,159
Do not expect me to believe you now.

561
00:46:55,840 --> 00:46:58,479
I've rebuilt all the walls..

562
00:46:58,640 --> 00:47:00,959
...that I broke for you, Trickster.

563
00:47:01,800 --> 00:47:03,759
Gonca Hatun.

564
00:47:07,760 --> 00:47:10,239
I won't let my heart speak anymore.

565
00:47:11,200 --> 00:47:13,359
It’s over.

566
00:47:18,600 --> 00:47:20,199
I know.

567
00:47:20,360 --> 00:47:23,359
But don't make it end like this, Alaaddin.

568
00:47:24,120 --> 00:47:26,239
Just listen to me.

569
00:47:26,520 --> 00:47:27,959
Then I'll go, anyway.

570
00:47:28,000 --> 00:47:31,559
You listened to your mother and
betrayed me| You became a spy, Goncai

571
00:47:31,600 --> 00:47:35,639
I didn’t! Alaaddin, I didn’t!

572
00:47:36,160 --> 00:47:38,839
Once! I swear...

573
00:47:38,840 --> 00:47:42,479
...I had to do it only once!

574
00:47:45,320 --> 00:47:48,479
You always say duties matter most.

575
00:47:48,720 --> 00:47:50,759
And you keep silent.

576
00:47:51,000 --> 00:47:53,079
Please see this as a duty!

577
00:47:53,120 --> 00:47:56,399
Your duty was me; It was me!

578
00:47:57,320 --> 00:48:00,079
Your duty was me!

579
00:48:03,320 --> 00:48:05,559
It was me.

580
00:48:08,520 --> 00:48:12,119
I accepted you as my dearest!

581
00:48:12,280 --> 00:48:14,639
I protected you from everything.

582
00:48:15,440 --> 00:48:17,319
You made your thorns bleed me!

583
00:48:17,640 --> 00:48:20,759
I will spit blood forever, Gonca Hatun!

584
00:48:25,560 --> 00:48:27,839
Don't talk like this, Alaaddin.

585
00:48:31,320 --> 00:48:34,879
You said it’d be hard but we'd
overcome hardships together.

586
00:48:37,240 --> 00:48:40,679
I believed in you and us.

587
00:48:43,400 --> 00:48:45,279
You know what?

588
00:48:45,520 --> 00:48:48,199
I was so scared before.

589
00:48:49,000 --> 00:48:52,279
But I thought our love could
overcome any hardships.

590
00:48:53,320 --> 00:48:56,359
I thought you would believe me.

591
00:48:57,200 --> 00:48:59,639
And then what happened?

592
00:48:59,760 --> 00:49:03,279
It's you who falls down
against the first hardship!

593
00:49:04,400 --> 00:49:06,719
I would face any hardships with you.

594
00:49:07,240 --> 00:49:09,279
Any hardships.

595
00:49:12,240 --> 00:49:14,119
But you betrayed me.

596
00:49:14,160 --> 00:49:15,519
I didn’t.

597
00:49:15,680 --> 00:49:17,359
You betrayed us, Gonca.

598
00:49:17,400 --> 00:49:19,439
I didn’t.

599
00:49:24,480 --> 00:49:26,399
Now I have a duty.

600
00:49:26,800 --> 00:49:28,879
Get out of my way.

601
00:50:00,920 --> 00:50:03,919
I don't need to keep it anymore.

602
00:50:31,160 --> 00:50:33,999
You ruined everything!

603
00:50:35,600 --> 00:50:40,879
Everything! Everything!
Barbarians!

604
00:51:01,960 --> 00:51:04,399
Princess Maria.

605
00:51:05,160 --> 00:51:08,079
They can do anything to be allies, huh?

606
00:51:08,160 --> 00:51:11,599
Then we can’t give the princess
to Mongolians or Byzantine.

607
00:51:11,600 --> 00:51:12,759
-There shouldn't be an alliance.
-There won't be.

608
00:51:12,760 --> 00:51:13,999
-There shouldn’t be an alliance
-There won’t be.

609
00:51:14,560 --> 00:51:16,279
There won't be, Bala.

610
00:51:16,280 --> 00:51:18,839
But there is something wrong with the princess.

611
00:51:19,200 --> 00:51:20,599
You need to fin’d out what it is.

612
00:51:20,600 --> 00:51:21,959
You need to find out what it is.

613
00:51:22,720 --> 00:51:24,639
You must be hungry.

614
00:51:24,840 --> 00:51:28,119
We’ve brought you food.
Kismet Hatun.

615
00:51:35,120 --> 00:51:37,719
You've been our guest for long, but...

616
00:51:37,920 --> 00:51:39,999
...we didn't meet before.

617
00:51:41,720 --> 00:51:45,599
I'm Bala Hatun, Osman Bey's wife.

618
00:51:46,040 --> 00:51:47,919
A guest?

619
00:51:48,200 --> 00:51:50,239
Do you always treat your guests like this?

620
00:51:50,240 --> 00:51:54,719
You’ve been dragging me around for days!

621
00:51:56,480 --> 00:52:01,439
We're doing this for your good, princess.

622
00:52:02,080 --> 00:52:05,999
We got rid of a man like Gorklu Khan thanks to us.

623
00:52:06,360 --> 00:52:08,319
My good?

624
00:52:08,640 --> 00:52:11,879
You ruined everything!

625
00:52:12,640 --> 00:52:15,359
All my plans failed!

626
00:52:15,920 --> 00:52:18,759
I was going to marry Gorklu Khan.

627
00:52:26,000 --> 00:52:28,719
You keep calling us barbarians.

628
00:52:29,400 --> 00:52:32,839
The real barbarian was Gorklu Khan.

629
00:52:33,360 --> 00:52:34,999
Don't tell me..

630
00:52:35,080 --> 00:52:37,719
...you'd marry such a man with your own will.

631
00:52:37,840 --> 00:52:40,679
I won’t believe that, princess.

632
00:52:44,280 --> 00:52:49,039
I was going to have this marriage
for Great Byzantine Empire.

633
00:52:51,200 --> 00:52:53,919
You can't understand me.

634
00:52:54,560 --> 00:52:57,599
Great Byzantine, huh?

635
00:52:58,200 --> 00:53:00,439
What you call Great Byzantine...

636
00:53:00,680 --> 00:53:04,719
...send you around like an item, princess.

637
00:53:06,960 --> 00:53:10,719
Open your ears and hear me well.

638
00:53:13,040 --> 00:53:15,439
Gorklu Khan is dead.

639
00:53:15,760 --> 00:53:20,519
Now they want to make you marry Tajeddin Noyan.

640
00:53:29,720 --> 00:53:32,199
Tajeddin Noyan?

641
00:53:33,480 --> 00:53:37,119
They keep changing the man you'll marry...

642
00:53:37,440 --> 00:53:40,519
...without asking you and taking your consent.

643
00:53:43,080 --> 00:53:46,239
How could you accept this?

644
00:53:48,640 --> 00:53:51,799
But it's not what we agreed.

645
00:53:53,160 --> 00:53:55,879
No, it can't be.

646
00:53:56,920 --> 00:53:58,919
Princess.

647
00:53:59,480 --> 00:54:02,439
You have a different issue.

648
00:54:08,880 --> 00:54:11,199
You can trust me.

649
00:54:20,240 --> 00:54:23,519
Can you please leave me alone?

650
00:54:51,200 --> 00:54:54,519
My Bey, Lord is coming.

651
00:54:55,600 --> 00:54:57,799
Come on

652
00:55:40,400 --> 00:55:42,519
Lord!

653
00:55:42,640 --> 00:55:44,999
-We were waiting for you!
-What for?

654
00:55:45,080 --> 00:55:47,719
You have an account to give us!

655
00:55:49,600 --> 00:55:53,359
Alps, attack!

656
00:55:53,760 --> 00:55:57,359
Come on

657
00:56:11,880 --> 00:56:14,959
Still no news from Lord Leon?

658
00:56:15,360 --> 00:56:18,439
We know they're marching to Atranos.

659
00:56:21,480 --> 00:56:23,759
-What's going on, soldier?
-My Lord.

660
00:56:23,880 --> 00:56:25,679
Osman's commander Konur..

661
00:56:25,800 --> 00:56:28,959
...besieged Atranos with his alps.

662
00:56:41,400 --> 00:56:43,599
Tell soldiers to take battle formation.

663
00:56:43,600 --> 00:56:47,279
Reinforce the gates! I want archers
on the walls and in the inner castle.

664
00:56:47,280 --> 00:56:47,959
Come on!

665
00:56:55,760 --> 00:56:58,039
Feel at ease, my friends.

666
00:56:58,160 --> 00:57:01,039
AtranoS walls are impassable.

667
00:57:02,000 --> 00:57:04,639
Although the walls are impassable,

668
00:57:04,880 --> 00:57:08,319
...Osman will find a way
in if he wants to get inside.

669
00:57:09,000 --> 00:57:11,919
Close the doors of the secret passage.

670
00:57:12,520 --> 00:57:15,999
Soldiers, do what she said.

671
00:57:18,000 --> 00:57:20,079
Well thought, Olivia.

672
00:57:20,200 --> 00:57:24,279
Osman will try those tunnels like a rat.

673
00:57:24,480 --> 00:57:27,599
He wouldn't come though
the gate of Great Atranos.

674
00:58:08,800 --> 00:58:10,759
Lord.

675
00:58:10,960 --> 00:58:14,079
You're out of breath, Lord.

676
00:58:15,320 --> 00:58:18,799
But we aren't barbarians as you think.

677
00:58:19,160 --> 00:58:21,199
We need you.

678
00:58:21,280 --> 00:58:22,279
Yagiz Alp. Kirbag.

679
00:58:26,560 --> 00:58:28,679
Take this.

680
00:58:28,840 --> 00:58:31,719
You must be thirsty.

681
00:58:37,720 --> 00:58:41,439
Drink it. Drink it.

682
00:58:50,840 --> 00:58:54,159
Why are you not killing me, Osman Bey?

683
00:58:54,760 --> 00:58:57,999
How do you know I didn't kill you?

684
00:58:59,960 --> 00:59:02,879
The water you just drank is poisonous.

685
00:59:05,640 --> 00:59:09,119
You... What have you done?

686
00:59:11,320 --> 00:59:13,239
How could you do this?

687
00:59:13,720 --> 00:59:16,319
Bring him.

688
00:59:29,400 --> 00:59:33,069
Mongol Captive Camp

689
00:59:42,960 --> 00:59:45,759
They are not like Mongolians.

690
00:59:45,960 --> 00:59:48,159
Samil.

691
00:59:48,520 --> 00:59:50,959
In the Mongolian army,

692
00:59:51,120 --> 00:59:53,199
...there are various tribes...

693
00:59:53,360 --> 00:59:56,399
...who scattered away from the llkhanid State.

694
00:59:57,560 --> 01:00:00,359
You heard Elcim Hatun.

695
01:00:01,280 --> 01:00:07,759
There are also Hasan Sabbah's
followers among them now.

696
01:00:12,760 --> 01:00:15,439
Our job has always been hard.

697
01:00:15,760 --> 01:00:18,319
But it's much harder now.

698
01:00:25,120 --> 01:00:26,879
Orhan Bey.

699
01:00:27,040 --> 01:00:29,039
You think this plan will work?

700
01:00:29,240 --> 01:00:31,599
What if it doesn’t, Elcim Hatun?

701
01:00:32,120 --> 01:00:35,199
We will just lose our lives, right?

702
01:00:37,040 --> 01:00:41,039
-Yes, but...
-If you are afraid,

703
01:00:41,400 --> 01:00:42,719
...stay back.

704
01:00:43,360 --> 01:00:47,119
we grew up with the smell of the
blood Mongolians shed, Orhan Bey.

705
01:00:47,280 --> 01:00:49,919
Not in palaces.

706
01:00:50,360 --> 01:00:53,079
We can hold on.

707
01:00:55,880 --> 01:00:58,399
Then, play well.

708
01:00:58,720 --> 01:01:01,999
Come on.

709
01:01:10,040 --> 01:01:13,399
-Everyone to positions!
-Was Nicea and Prusa informed?

710
01:01:13,560 --> 01:01:15,439
Alps can not exit, my Lord.

711
01:01:15,480 --> 01:01:17,799
The castle is completely surrounded.

712
01:01:17,880 --> 01:01:19,639
Turks are coming!

713
01:01:19,920 --> 01:01:22,879
Just a couple of horsemen;

714
01:01:23,240 --> 01:01:25,399
Is it Osman?

715
01:01:33,640 --> 01:01:37,079
Tell your Lords, Osman Bey has arrived!

716
01:01:37,600 --> 01:01:40,519
Open the doors!

717
01:01:49,120 --> 01:01:51,679
What a confidence Osman hast

718
01:01:51,880 --> 01:01:55,559
-He must have something.
-The Lord of Kite is in our hands!

719
01:01:55,840 --> 01:01:57,679
Now, either open the doors..

720
01:01:57,880 --> 01:02:00,879
..or we will destroy them!

721
01:02:07,840 --> 01:02:09,599
Come.

722
01:02:14,520 --> 01:02:16,399
Here!

723
01:02:16,640 --> 01:02:20,439
I brought the Lord! Open the gates!

724
01:02:24,320 --> 01:02:27,599
Open the gates!

725
01:02:44,600 --> 01:02:46,799
Never!

726
01:02:48,040 --> 01:02:50,599
I will never allow him inside my castle!

727
01:02:50,680 --> 01:02:52,959
He has Lord Leon.

728
01:02:53,240 --> 01:02:56,159
Let him in. He can not do anything by himself.

729
01:02:56,360 --> 01:02:59,199
We have the upper hand here.

730
01:03:10,440 --> 01:03:12,679
He has the Lord of Kite.

731
01:03:12,960 --> 01:03:15,839
Let him in.

732
01:03:16,200 --> 01:03:18,479
Soldiers!

733
01:03:18,640 --> 01:03:20,999
Open the gates!

734
01:03:37,440 --> 01:03:40,359
Have you never heard what happens..

735
01:03:40,560 --> 01:03:43,519
..to those who do wrong to us?

736
01:03:45,520 --> 01:03:47,639
Here.

737
01:03:50,640 --> 01:03:52,439
Now.

738
01:03:52,680 --> 01:03:55,439
He will tell you how he sold you out..

739
01:03:55,640 --> 01:03:58,839
..how he betrayed you!

740
01:03:59,520 --> 01:04:03,399
However, you will not like it.

741
01:04:27,560 --> 01:04:30,639
Come on.

742
01:04:38,720 --> 01:04:40,959
Nokers!

743
01:04:41,480 --> 01:04:43,839
We are not enemy.

744
01:04:44,000 --> 01:04:47,039
We brought the captive you couldn't catch.

745
01:04:47,320 --> 01:04:49,199
Aren't you looking for this girl?

746
01:04:49,320 --> 01:04:53,159
We are, but who are you?

747
01:04:56,200 --> 01:04:58,079
Father?

748
01:04:59,760 --> 01:05:02,639
Elcim Hatun.

749
01:05:02,720 --> 01:05:04,439
Don’t expose yourself.

750
01:05:04,520 --> 01:05:08,279
Come on, get ahold of yourself.

751
01:05:22,400 --> 01:05:25,759
We are the alps Tajeddin
Noyan gathered from frontiers!

752
01:05:26,080 --> 01:05:29,319
If you strike us..

753
01:05:29,800 --> 01:05:32,999
..he will not let any of you live.

754
01:05:33,920 --> 01:05:35,719
Now..

755
01:05:35,960 --> 01:05:41,719
Tajeddin Noyan promised
us gold in return of this captive.

756
01:05:42,040 --> 01:05:44,239
Now give us our gold.

757
01:05:44,240 --> 01:05:46,199
We will give you your gold.

758
01:05:46,240 --> 01:05:48,319
However, give us the girl first.

759
01:05:48,920 --> 01:05:51,559
Stop there.

760
01:05:52,720 --> 01:05:56,919
The only thing we will give you..

761
01:05:56,960 --> 01:05:58,999
..is the cold steel of our swords.

762
01:05:59,000 --> 01:06:02,239
Alps!

763
01:07:03,880 --> 01:07:06,279
Elcim Hatuni

764
01:07:07,120 --> 01:07:09,759
Now..

765
01:07:10,680 --> 01:07:12,199
Tell them everything.

766
01:07:12,560 --> 01:07:15,039
Why would a person who knows he will die..

767
01:07:15,120 --> 01:07:18,079
..tell everything?

768
01:07:23,760 --> 01:07:25,879
You will tell..

769
01:07:25,920 --> 01:07:28,039
..if you need to tell..

770
01:07:28,640 --> 01:07:31,559
..to live.

771
01:07:41,920 --> 01:07:44,159
Here.

772
01:07:44,840 --> 01:07:47,639
Do you know what is inside bf this?

773
01:07:49,760 --> 01:07:52,839
This has your cure in it.

774
01:07:53,040 --> 01:07:55,719
The antidote.

775
01:07:58,120 --> 01:07:59,679
Osman Bey!

776
01:07:59,720 --> 01:08:03,119
-Stop there.
-Osman Bey, the antidote!

777
01:08:03,120 --> 01:08:05,919
Stop there, stop!

778
01:08:05,960 --> 01:08:07,919
Now..

779
01:08:08,680 --> 01:08:12,039
You will tell them everything.

780
01:08:12,360 --> 01:08:15,039
Emir Gorklu Khan sent me a messenger.

781
01:08:15,120 --> 01:08:16,839
To serve him.

782
01:08:17,319 --> 01:08:19,759
Phelped him against Osman Bey.

783
01:08:20,200 --> 01:08:21,959
Osman Bey, give the antidote!

784
01:08:21,960 --> 01:08:24,198
Osman Bey!

785
01:08:24,800 --> 01:08:29,318
Osman Bey! The antidote!

786
01:08:29,960 --> 01:08:32,999
Tell them how you betrayed your friends.

787
01:08:37,840 --> 01:08:40,238
I cannot say more.

788
01:08:49,240 --> 01:08:51,719
You wanted this.

789
01:08:52,040 --> 01:08:54,238
Osman Bey, alright!

790
01:08:54,439 --> 01:08:57,439
Alright.

791
01:08:58,680 --> 01:09:00,398
Emir Gorklu Khan..

792
01:09:00,600 --> 01:09:04,238
He was going to take every castle of Lords.

793
01:09:05,000 --> 01:09:08,799
And you sided with him knowing that?

794
01:09:09,040 --> 01:09:14,318
Osman Bey, give me the antidote!

795
01:09:14,560 --> 01:09:17,078
It is not over!

796
01:09:17,960 --> 01:09:19,879
Tell them.

797
01:09:20,160 --> 01:09:23,238
Gorklu Khan, after taking the castles..

798
01:09:23,880 --> 01:09:29,198
..he was going to give them all
to me, that's why I helped him.

799
01:09:29,720 --> 01:09:32,118
Osman Bey, there is not much time!

800
01:09:32,120 --> 01:09:34,639
I will die! Give me that antidote!

801
01:09:34,680 --> 01:09:37,519
Osman Bey!

802
01:09:37,800 --> 01:09:41,037
Get off!

803
01:09:41,920 --> 01:09:44,278
So you want the antidote.

804
01:09:50,040 --> 01:09:52,479
..you want this.

805
01:10:01,240 --> 01:10:04,799
What did you do?

806
01:10:05,000 --> 01:10:08,919
This was my last chance to live!

807
01:10:09,360 --> 01:10:13,919
Lord.

808
01:10:15,040 --> 01:10:19,359
The thing you drank, was only water.

809
01:10:24,360 --> 01:10:27,599
There was no poison in it.

810
01:10:28,560 --> 01:10:31,199
The thing that circles your blood..

811
01:10:31,240 --> 01:10:34,679
..is only fear of death.

812
01:11:12,520 --> 01:11:14,839
Father.

813
01:11:47,320 --> 01:11:50,199
We were late, Orhan Bey.

814
01:11:50,520 --> 01:11:53,079
We were late.

815
01:12:01,080 --> 01:12:03,559
Elcim Hatun.

816
01:13:03,120 --> 01:13:05,359
He is not my father.

817
01:13:07,360 --> 01:13:09,679
What?

818
01:13:10,160 --> 01:13:11,999
He is not my father, Orhan Bey.

819
01:13:12,080 --> 01:13:14,159
My Allah.

820
01:13:14,440 --> 01:13:16,919
My Allah, thank you.

821
01:13:21,000 --> 01:13:23,239
Orhan...

822
01:13:23,280 --> 01:13:26,519
No one will take you from me today!

823
01:13:26,600 --> 01:13:29,039
Karacelasun.

824
01:13:29,040 --> 01:13:32,639
Now I will take your life!

825
01:13:36,840 --> 01:13:39,239
This time..

826
01:13:39,680 --> 01:13:43,079
..this time you won’t get away!

827
01:13:43,560 --> 01:13:46,039
First, tell me.

828
01:13:46,120 --> 01:13:48,039
Where is Gunduz Bey?

829
01:13:48,080 --> 01:13:49,719
Nokersi

830
01:13:49,880 --> 01:13:51,479
Leave none of them alivet

831
01:13:51,640 --> 01:13:55,319
-Alps!
-Ya Allah!

832
01:13:55,360 --> 01:13:58,279
I am leaving this dog to you.

833
01:14:21,760 --> 01:14:24,399
I won’t kill this dog.

834
01:14:29,520 --> 01:14:33,559
So you sold your long friends to Mongols.

835
01:14:36,960 --> 01:14:39,079
A noble Lord of..

836
01:14:39,360 --> 01:14:41,279
..Roman Empire is..

837
01:14:41,360 --> 01:14:43,959
..being humiliated in front of you.

838
01:14:44,480 --> 01:14:46,479
You don't even move;

839
01:14:47,520 --> 01:14:51,559
You should've thought about
that before selling Rome out.

840
01:14:56,280 --> 01:14:59,919
Was I the only one?

841
01:15:00,520 --> 01:15:02,399
Do you think..

842
01:15:02,480 --> 01:15:04,439
.. I am the only one?

843
01:15:33,680 --> 01:15:35,999
What do you want from us, Osman Bey?

844
01:15:36,040 --> 01:15:39,719
The tax you promised to pay.

845
01:15:42,160 --> 01:15:43,919
Right now.

846
01:15:43,920 --> 01:15:47,039
Osman Bey... We cannot pay you in a week!

847
01:15:47,120 --> 01:15:48,799
Today!

848
01:15:48,840 --> 01:15:51,159
You will pay it today!

849
01:15:51,400 --> 01:15:53,719
Or else..

850
01:15:53,800 --> 01:15:56,119
I will take your properties...

851
01:15:56,360 --> 01:15:59,119
...as a cost.

852
01:16:04,320 --> 01:16:08,159
And this is my last warning.

853
01:16:22,560 --> 01:16:25,999
There is no other way, Lords!

854
01:16:26,400 --> 01:16:28,959
I will send a letter to the Emperor.

855
01:16:29,000 --> 01:16:32,199
What are you going to say, Olivia?

856
01:16:33,160 --> 01:16:35,799
I will ask him to send..

857
01:16:38,280 --> 01:16:42,239
...the Executioner of Roman Empire with his men.

858
01:16:43,320 --> 01:16:45,839
If the Executioner of Roman Empire comes...

859
01:16:45,960 --> 01:16:47,359
...not only Osman...

860
01:16:47,560 --> 01:16:51,599
...but everyone living on this land
will suffer more than they ever did.

861
01:16:51,600 --> 01:16:54,839
We cannot stop the Executioner
of Roman Empire, Olivia!

862
01:16:55,120 --> 01:16:57,319
I know.

863
01:16:57,680 --> 01:17:01,679
I know that even the Emperor
cannot make him listen.

864
01:17:01,760 --> 01:17:04,439
I did not forget what he did.

865
01:17:04,760 --> 01:17:07,799
But we have no other choice!

866
01:17:08,000 --> 01:17:10,839
Roman Empire was founded on these sacrifices.

867
01:17:11,720 --> 01:17:15,959
And it will live forever with those sacrifices.

868
01:17:17,160 --> 01:17:21,679
Only the Executioner of Roman
Empire can defeat Osman.

869
01:17:39,480 --> 01:17:42,279
If he comes...

870
01:17:42,880 --> 01:17:44,999
...Orhan...

871
01:17:46,520 --> 01:17:48,879
They will all die.

872
01:18:34,800 --> 01:18:41,159
Stand up!

873
01:18:41,520 --> 01:18:43,199
You will pay the price of...

874
01:18:43,320 --> 01:18:45,719
...what you did to my family and my people!

875
01:18:47,720 --> 01:18:52,119
Stop...

876
01:18:56,000 --> 01:18:59,079
Stand up!

877
01:18:59,560 --> 01:19:01,479
You dog... Today...

878
01:19:01,480 --> 01:19:05,399
...I told you that you wouldn't
be able to escape from me.

879
01:19:05,520 --> 01:19:08,159
Now, Karacelasun..

880
01:19:08,280 --> 01:19:10,799
...you will either speak here...

881
01:19:10,920 --> 01:19:13,519
..or I will cut your head off!

882
01:19:13,880 --> 01:19:17,159
Speak, you dastard; Where is my father?

883
01:19:17,200 --> 01:19:21,319
-Where is my aunt? Speak!
-Stop, Elcim Hatun!

884
01:19:26,240 --> 01:19:28,439
Speak!

885
01:19:28,920 --> 01:19:32,399
Do you think you can find them?

886
01:19:32,520 --> 01:19:34,399
Tajeddin Noyan..

887
01:19:34,520 --> 01:19:36,919
...prepared such a death for them that...

888
01:19:37,240 --> 01:19:38,879
-Tell me!
-Elcim Hatun!

889
01:19:38,920 --> 01:19:41,279
Tell me, or I will rip your heart out!

890
01:19:41,360 --> 01:19:44,639
Hatun... I told you to stop.

891
01:19:45,480 --> 01:19:47,559
Calm down.

892
01:19:50,040 --> 01:19:53,879
My Shahzade. I know how to make this dog speak.

893
01:19:53,960 --> 01:19:57,119
Allow me to make him speak.

894
01:19:59,120 --> 01:20:01,399
We will make this dog speak!

895
01:20:01,880 --> 01:20:03,959
But not here..

896
01:20:04,520 --> 01:20:07,039
We will make him speak in Yenisehir.

897
01:20:07,400 --> 01:20:10,999
Bayindir Bey! Take this dastard dog to Yenisehir.

898
01:20:11,520 --> 01:20:13,079
He will wait in the dungeon.

899
01:20:13,120 --> 01:20:16,719
Don't worry about that, my Shahzade.

900
01:20:17,000 --> 01:20:19,119
He will not die..

901
01:20:19,240 --> 01:20:21,999
...before he says something important.

902
01:20:22,240 --> 01:20:23,719
Elcim Hatun..

903
01:20:24,360 --> 01:20:26,439
We will learn where your father...

904
01:20:26,680 --> 01:20:29,359
...and aunt are from this dog.

905
01:20:29,640 --> 01:20:31,359
We will make him speak.

906
01:20:31,640 --> 01:20:34,879
But first, we will go to Yenisehir.

907
01:20:43,480 --> 01:20:45,399
Alps!

908
01:20:47,200 --> 01:20:50,599
Take our martyrs down from there.

909
01:20:52,400 --> 01:20:55,519
Come on.

910
01:21:07,080 --> 01:21:10,679
My Allah, may You give relief to my heart.

911
01:21:27,080 --> 01:21:29,879
Let's have some rest here.

912
01:22:07,420 --> 01:22:13,059
May you be safe from evil,
and mercy of Allah be upon you.

913
01:22:25,800 --> 01:22:29,079
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you too.

914
01:22:29,320 --> 01:22:31,439
May Allah accept it.

915
01:22:31,520 --> 01:22:33,119
We didn't see you here.

916
01:22:33,120 --> 01:22:35,919
-I hope we are not disturbing you.
-Not at all.

917
01:22:35,920 --> 01:22:37,319
Here.

918
01:22:42,400 --> 01:22:44,559
Thank you.

919
01:22:51,400 --> 01:22:54,159
I saw you when you came to the palace.

920
01:22:54,280 --> 01:22:55,999
Yunus Emre..

921
01:22:56,000 --> 01:22:57,559
My Osman Bey...

922
01:22:57,680 --> 01:23:00,039
...and my Orhan told me a lot about you.

923
01:23:00,080 --> 01:23:02,239
We were destined to meet today.

924
01:23:02,280 --> 01:23:04,159
Right...

925
01:23:04,200 --> 01:23:08,279
It is our destiny to see, it
is our destiny to be seen.

926
01:23:09,840 --> 01:23:12,959
Even a herb cannot grow without destiny.

927
01:23:19,640 --> 01:23:22,359
You cannot walk on a way without it.

928
01:23:24,160 --> 01:23:27,799
If you are destined to go somewhere...

929
01:23:27,920 --> 01:23:32,359
...nothing can stop you from going there.

930
01:23:35,200 --> 01:23:39,519
What if we are not sure?

931
01:23:44,840 --> 01:23:47,719
I had a dream, Yunus Emre.

932
01:23:48,000 --> 01:23:50,879
In my dream, I saw bandits on one side...

933
01:23:51,280 --> 01:23:54,919
...and the way of pilgrimage on the other side.

934
01:23:55,880 --> 01:23:58,559
But I am not sure.

935
01:23:58,640 --> 01:24:00,919
Is it better to go...

936
01:24:01,160 --> 01:24:04,319
...or to stay?

937
01:24:05,560 --> 01:24:07,919
Our Allah says: "There is evil in good...

938
01:24:08,120 --> 01:24:11,719
...and there is good in evil.”

939
01:24:12,240 --> 01:24:15,639
You cannot know that before
you set out, Malhun Hatun.

940
01:24:16,120 --> 01:24:19,279
But you are talking about the way of pilgrimage.

941
01:24:19,600 --> 01:24:22,879
The way of pilgrimage is the way of love.

942
01:24:23,000 --> 01:24:25,879
It is the way that goes to Rasulullah (PBUH)

943
01:24:27,560 --> 01:24:31,119
Even if there is a test on that path...

944
01:24:31,240 --> 01:24:32,639
...it is also a blessing.

945
01:24:32,680 --> 01:24:34,439
Allah knows my heart.

946
01:24:34,560 --> 01:24:37,959
Every time I think about the Kaaba,
my feelings defeat my wisdom.

947
01:24:38,160 --> 01:24:41,719
There is such a longing inside me...

948
01:24:42,840 --> 01:24:45,199
Of course, I am willing to take the test.

949
01:24:45,280 --> 01:24:48,319
But what I really think about is...

950
01:24:49,360 --> 01:24:53,279
Am I worthy of putting my face on Beytullah?

951
01:24:54,560 --> 01:24:56,359
What if I'm not?

952
01:24:57,320 --> 01:25:01,839
Do you think that's why horsemen
were chasing me in my dreams?

953
01:25:02,040 --> 01:25:05,119
If Allah calls someone to His presence...

954
01:25:05,600 --> 01:25:09,079
...who can prevent His servant from going there?

955
01:25:09,480 --> 01:25:13,479
As you worry about being worthy enough or not...

956
01:25:13,560 --> 01:25:17,199
...you might be preparing yourself for that way.

957
01:25:17,520 --> 01:25:21,079
You purify your heart from desire and ambition.

958
01:25:21,200 --> 01:25:23,239
You are running away from your...

959
01:25:23,320 --> 01:25:27,039
...nafs and the dirt of the world.

960
01:25:27,400 --> 01:25:30,439
Maybe those bandits...

961
01:25:30,520 --> 01:25:33,279
...were showing this to you.

962
01:25:36,040 --> 01:25:38,639
We don't know.

963
01:25:39,760 --> 01:25:43,599
Now... if you are looking for an answer...

964
01:25:44,080 --> 01:25:47,079
...you will ask it to your heart.

965
01:25:48,520 --> 01:25:50,959
It is your heart that will tell you...

966
01:25:51,160 --> 01:25:53,719
...the meaning of your dream.

967
01:25:54,320 --> 01:25:57,439
I know what my heart says.

968
01:25:57,840 --> 01:26:01,319
When I saw myself in that ihram..

969
01:26:02,240 --> 01:26:06,639
...every way other than
Kaaba is a foreign land for me.

970
01:26:09,360 --> 01:26:10,079
And now...

971
01:26:10,120 --> 01:26:14,399
...I will try hard to be granted with
being worthy enough by my Allah...

972
01:26:14,480 --> 01:26:16,719
...and set out, if Allah permits.

973
01:26:17,320 --> 01:26:18,719
Then..

974
01:26:19,200 --> 01:26:22,039
...may Allah let you go there safely.

975
01:26:22,280 --> 01:26:24,759
Aameen.

976
01:26:44,000 --> 01:26:46,559
Princess Maria.

977
01:26:51,040 --> 01:26:53,759
I heard that you have not been eating anything.

978
01:26:53,760 --> 01:26:58,079
I had different meals prepared
for you. You might like these, huh?

979
01:27:06,240 --> 01:27:09,479
What are you going to do to me, Bala Hatun?

980
01:27:09,880 --> 01:27:12,559
If you send me to Byzantium...

981
01:27:12,600 --> 01:27:15,559
...they will send me to Tajeddin Noyan.

982
01:27:15,600 --> 01:27:18,719
You will lose.

983
01:27:20,920 --> 01:27:25,399
My presence here is dangerous for you.

984
01:27:28,560 --> 01:27:31,159
Will you kill me?

985
01:27:35,120 --> 01:27:39,679
You really think we are barbaric people, huh?

986
01:27:41,240 --> 01:27:44,199
You are our guest, Princess.

987
01:27:44,440 --> 01:27:47,399
The life of our guest...

988
01:27:49,360 --> 01:27:53,159
...is entrusted to us. We will protect you.

989
01:27:56,240 --> 01:27:59,759
You were right, Bala Hatun.

990
01:28:00,440 --> 01:28:03,959
I was not willing to marry Gorklu Khan

991
01:28:04,480 --> 01:28:06,479
They threatened me.

992
01:28:06,800 --> 01:28:08,559
Threatened you?

993
01:28:11,160 --> 01:28:14,039
I love a Turk.

994
01:28:15,680 --> 01:28:19,479
In the Constantine..

995
01:28:19,560 --> 01:28:22,479
I met him when he w£s working as a merchant...

996
01:28:22,680 --> 01:28:25,519
We were going to run away, but....

997
01:28:26,840 --> 01:28:28,959
...we could not.

998
01:28:29,360 --> 01:28:32,759
They took him captive.

999
01:28:33,920 --> 01:28:37,279
They are going to kill him if I don’t marry him.

1000
01:28:38,120 --> 01:28:42,079
Only you can help me, please.

1001
01:28:54,480 --> 01:28:58,639
Attention! Osman Bey!

1002
01:29:00,520 --> 01:29:04,319
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you too.

1003
01:29:13,080 --> 01:29:15,599
You can sit down.

1004
01:29:25,680 --> 01:29:28,719
I am starting the council meeting with the...

1005
01:29:28,760 --> 01:29:31,639
...99 Names of Almighty Allah...

1006
01:29:31,800 --> 01:29:35,159
...Who holds us responsible for the war...

1007
01:29:35,360 --> 01:29:37,919
...not the victory.

1008
01:29:38,040 --> 01:29:44,519
In the name of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate.

1009
01:29:46,040 --> 01:29:48,439
Now we are becoming a state.

1010
01:29:48,960 --> 01:29:54,559
Everything will be harder than before.

1011
01:29:57,400 --> 01:30:00,399
Mehmet Bey...

1012
01:30:00,640 --> 01:30:02,919
Tell me.

1013
01:30:03,040 --> 01:30:06,439
What makes the state exist?

1014
01:30:08,200 --> 01:30:10,239
Morals.

1015
01:30:11,280 --> 01:30:14,239
Morals, right.

1016
01:30:14,480 --> 01:30:17,439
Of course, we will protect our morals.

1017
01:30:17,680 --> 01:30:21,079
And everyone, everyone will...

1018
01:30:21,320 --> 01:30:23,959
...secure justice in their lands.

1019
01:30:26,080 --> 01:30:28,159
No one..

1020
01:30:28,240 --> 01:30:31,759
...no one will attempt doing
something behind our back.

1021
01:30:35,760 --> 01:30:38,759
If justice cannot be secured..

1022
01:30:38,880 --> 01:30:43,039
...then the light of that state...

1023
01:30:43,280 --> 01:30:45,319
...is about to fade.

1024
01:30:45,360 --> 01:30:47,159
Know that.

1025
01:30:49,240 --> 01:30:52,199
Everyone understood that
one cannot build a state...

1026
01:30:52,320 --> 01:30:55,919
...with gold...

1027
01:30:56,120 --> 01:30:59,199
...and Alps.

1028
01:31:02,760 --> 01:31:05,759
Osman Bey!

1029
01:31:06,080 --> 01:31:08,799
Did you gather the Beys for a council...

1030
01:31:08,960 --> 01:31:11,239
...or a ceremony to humiliate us?

1031
01:31:11,320 --> 01:31:13,679
Mehmeti

1032
01:31:14,400 --> 01:31:17,559
e are not humiliating you, Mehmet Bey!

1033
01:31:17,600 --> 01:31:21,559
-We are trying to take you out of the hole...
-Alaeddin...

1034
01:31:50,000 --> 01:31:52,759
Beys...

1035
01:31:55,720 --> 01:31:58,319
We are mortals.

1036
01:31:58,480 --> 01:32:02,119
Sooner or later, we will all pass away.

1037
01:32:02,240 --> 01:32:06,399
But... but our dream..

1038
01:32:06,480 --> 01:32:09,399
...is longer than a lifetime.

1039
01:32:09,480 --> 01:32:12,879
Do not forget that.

1040
01:32:18,480 --> 01:32:21,799
Tell me Yakup Bey!

1041
01:32:25,280 --> 01:32:27,759
What is our goal?

1042
01:32:32,680 --> 01:32:34,959
Our purpose..

1043
01:32:35,040 --> 01:32:37,679
..is to spread the name of Allah..

1044
01:32:37,720 --> 01:32:40,399
..to the whole World.

1045
01:32:51,720 --> 01:32:53,639
That is why..

1046
01:32:54,040 --> 01:33:00,559
..no one will try to rise the
banner alone with arrogance.

1047
01:33:02,440 --> 01:33:05,399
As..

1048
01:33:06,000 --> 01:33:10,119
..this would not fit to any muslim.

1049
01:33:18,960 --> 01:33:20,999
Of course..

1050
01:33:21,400 --> 01:33:24,719
..everyone will do what is needed.

1051
01:33:26,280 --> 01:33:30,599
And we will have the heads of those who does not.

1052
01:33:38,480 --> 01:33:41,279
Osman Bey.

1053
01:33:41,840 --> 01:33:45,039
We heard what we heard.

1054
01:33:45,360 --> 01:33:48,519
And got we got.

1055
01:33:49,760 --> 01:33:51,919
However..

1056
01:33:52,040 --> 01:33:55,559
..you always told us about state...

1057
01:33:55,640 --> 01:33:58,399
...about tradition.

1058
01:33:59,680 --> 01:34:01,359
What about army

1059
01:34:02,040 --> 01:34:03,559
What about war?

1060
01:34:13,240 --> 01:34:16,279
Yakup Bey.

1061
01:34:23,000 --> 01:34:26,559
I will speak of them in a council
where you will not be present.

1062
01:34:41,360 --> 01:34:43,959
You will go back to your home.

1063
01:34:44,520 --> 01:34:49,319
Tajeddin Noyan targets both of us.

1064
01:34:51,400 --> 01:34:53,599
Kutahya is in his range.

1065
01:34:54,160 --> 01:34:58,519
You will prevent all attacks
that will come from there.

1066
01:35:02,120 --> 01:35:04,239
For now..

1067
01:35:07,120 --> 01:35:11,039
..for now that is enough.

1068
01:35:18,760 --> 01:35:21,919
-Father.
-Mehmed.

1069
01:35:27,520 --> 01:35:29,559
If this is appropriate..

1070
01:35:29,960 --> 01:35:32,959
..for our act..

1071
01:35:34,720 --> 01:35:37,919
..I won't hold back from doing it.

1072
01:35:38,040 --> 01:35:40,439
It is appropriate.

1073
01:35:53,320 --> 01:35:56,599
Since time has changed..

1074
01:35:56,920 --> 01:36:00,119
..then the war will not stay like this.

1075
01:36:00,760 --> 01:36:04,079
Of course it will grow.

1076
01:36:05,200 --> 01:36:08,079
Everyone, make your preparations.

1077
01:36:12,880 --> 01:36:15,239
Come.

1078
01:36:52,640 --> 01:36:56,519
-Peace be upon you, my Shahzade.
-Peace be upon you too, Solgur Aga.

1079
01:36:57,160 --> 01:36:57,959
Bayindir Bey..

1080
01:36:57,960 --> 01:37:01,959
..was going to bring that dog Karacelasun
to palace using secret passages.

1081
01:37:01,960 --> 01:37:04,959
-Did they arrive?
-They arrived, my Shahzade.

1082
01:37:05,160 --> 01:37:09,439
They will beat that dog mongol until he speaks.

1083
01:37:09,720 --> 01:37:12,079
Alright.

1084
01:37:12,240 --> 01:37:15,399
First, he will tell what he knows..

1085
01:37:15,760 --> 01:37:18,239
..then he will lose his life.

1086
01:37:18,600 --> 01:37:22,039
If Allah permits, my Shahzade.

1087
01:37:47,360 --> 01:37:49,039
We shouldn’t have come here.

1088
01:37:49,080 --> 01:37:50,679
If your aunt finds out..

1089
01:37:50,680 --> 01:37:52,519
Orhan took me for a fool, Andra.

1090
01:37:52,720 --> 01:37:56,119
He lied to me. He will pay for this.

1091
01:38:01,640 --> 01:38:03,359
There he is.

1092
01:38:03,400 --> 01:38:07,519
Let's see your answer, Shahzade.

1093
01:38:13,800 --> 01:38:15,679
Elcim Hatun.

1094
01:38:19,560 --> 01:38:20,879
Elcim Hatun.

1095
01:38:21,000 --> 01:38:24,679
Osman Bey is waiting for
you at the palace, where to?

1096
01:38:26,240 --> 01:38:28,199
Elcim Hatun?

1097
01:38:28,560 --> 01:38:29,799
Who is he?

1098
01:38:29,840 --> 01:38:32,759
I don't know. Let’s go.

1099
01:38:33,960 --> 01:38:36,359
Orhan Bey.

1100
01:38:36,440 --> 01:38:38,079
You go.

1101
01:38:38,320 --> 01:38:40,919
I will come later.

1102
01:38:41,320 --> 01:38:42,759
Are you..

1103
01:38:43,480 --> 01:38:45,559
..alright?

1104
01:38:47,520 --> 01:38:49,399
I am alright.

1105
01:38:50,000 --> 01:38:52,119
Its just that..

1106
01:38:55,000 --> 01:38:57,479
..I want to be alone.

1107
01:39:09,040 --> 01:39:11,359
Elcim Hatun.

1108
01:39:11,800 --> 01:39:14,279
It is hard, what you've been through.

1109
01:39:15,840 --> 01:39:17,919
Your father..

1110
01:39:18,000 --> 01:39:20,319
..your aunt..

1111
01:39:24,280 --> 01:39:28,199
..however, we did not
find their dead now, did we?

1112
01:39:33,280 --> 01:39:36,159
With Allah's permission, they're alive.

1113
01:39:43,840 --> 01:39:46,159
Elcim Hatun.

1114
01:39:46,240 --> 01:39:49,399
Wipe your tears.

1115
01:39:58,960 --> 01:40:01,959
There was nothing we could talk about anyways.

1116
01:40:02,080 --> 01:40:05,239
Orhan already made his choice it seems.

1117
01:40:06,600 --> 01:40:08,919
That mongol dog..

1118
01:40:09,000 --> 01:40:10,919
..is in our hands.

1119
01:40:10,960 --> 01:40:14,799
We will make him speak. Do not worry.

1120
01:40:16,000 --> 01:40:18,119
we will find your father..

1121
01:40:18,280 --> 01:40:20,839
..and your aunt.

1122
01:40:23,840 --> 01:40:26,919
Holofira?

1123
01:40:26,960 --> 01:40:29,999
What is she doing here?

1124
01:40:35,160 --> 01:40:38,839
-Brother.
-Sister.

1125
01:40:52,720 --> 01:40:53,799
What is it?

1126
01:40:53,840 --> 01:40:57,439
Brother, I just saw Holofira.

1127
01:40:58,720 --> 01:41:01,359
It seems she saw you both.

1128
01:41:06,000 --> 01:41:09,399
She went to the Yenisehir gates, crying.

1129
01:41:10,480 --> 01:41:11,999
Holofira..

1130
01:41:12,240 --> 01:41:15,199
Who knows what she thought.

1131
01:41:22,760 --> 01:41:24,919
Who is Holofira?

1132
01:41:25,120 --> 01:41:28,039
Besides, what did she even see?

1133
01:41:29,680 --> 01:41:32,559
She is his lover.

1134
01:41:33,880 --> 01:41:35,799
And you?

1135
01:41:36,360 --> 01:41:38,479
Who are you?

1136
01:41:38,800 --> 01:41:42,959
What are you doing with my
brother with these clothes?

1137
01:41:44,800 --> 01:41:47,999
I'm from Kayi Tribe and
descendant of Hayme Mother.

1138
01:41:48,280 --> 01:41:51,759
I'm Efendize Elcim Hatun.

1139
01:41:52,800 --> 01:41:55,679
See you in the palace, Fatma Hatun.

1140
01:42:03,880 --> 01:42:06,439
Don't look. Don't look back.

1141
01:42:06,600 --> 01:42:08,399
Holofira.

1142
01:42:09,080 --> 01:42:11,599
Holofira, it's not as you think!

1143
01:42:11,640 --> 01:42:13,679
Get out of my way! I don't want to see you.

1144
01:42:13,760 --> 01:42:17,199
Holofira, you're misjudging.
Nothing is as you see!

1145
01:42:17,480 --> 01:42:19,479
That's right.

1146
01:42:19,760 --> 01:42:22,559
You’re not as you seem at all.

1147
01:42:22,920 --> 01:42:25,599
You are just a liar.

1148
01:42:25,880 --> 01:42:28,199
Holofira.

1149
01:42:28,320 --> 01:42:31,079
You're saying things that you will regret.

1150
01:42:31,120 --> 01:42:33,039
Don't.

1151
01:42:33,720 --> 01:42:35,759
I can't explain this right now.

1152
01:42:36,080 --> 01:42:37,799
But know this.

1153
01:42:38,000 --> 01:42:42,079
I have nothing to do with that hatun.

1154
01:42:42,680 --> 01:42:44,679
What about the princess?

1155
01:42:45,000 --> 01:42:48,119
What about the game you
played for my aunt and me?

1156
01:42:48,440 --> 01:42:52,279
You lied to me looking into my eyes!

1157
01:42:52,720 --> 01:42:55,719
Although you knew my aunt would turn against you.

1158
01:42:56,000 --> 01:42:59,599
You separated us forever.

1159
01:43:04,360 --> 01:43:07,479
Nobody can separate us, Lord's daughter.

1160
01:43:10,760 --> 01:43:13,279
Just look at me.

1161
01:43:15,520 --> 01:43:19,439
Even you can’t get between
you and my love for you.

1162
01:43:20,840 --> 01:43:24,319
Look. I didn't lie to you.

1163
01:43:24,840 --> 01:43:27,719
It was my duty.

1164
01:43:27,840 --> 01:43:30,799
And I did what I needed to do.

1165
01:43:31,600 --> 01:43:33,679
Just words.

1166
01:43:33,840 --> 01:43:37,119
You only say words, Orhan.

1167
01:43:40,400 --> 01:43:43,359
You keep talking about duties.

1168
01:43:44,160 --> 01:43:46,639
I'll do you a last favor.

1169
01:43:47,360 --> 01:43:48,719
My aunt...

1170
01:43:48,920 --> 01:43:51,639
...sent a letter to the emperor.

1171
01:43:51,960 --> 01:43:54,759
the Executioner of Roman Empire is coming here.

1172
01:44:00,920 --> 01:44:03,279
Who is the Executioner of Roman Empire?

1173
01:44:04,440 --> 01:44:08,159
You started a great war, Orhan.

1174
01:44:10,800 --> 01:44:13,359
You made my aunt turn against you.

1175
01:44:13,960 --> 01:44:16,119
You didn’t put only our love...

1176
01:44:16,160 --> 01:44:18,719
..but also your people in dange

1177
01:44:19,160 --> 01:44:22,399
You can’t do anything for us anymore.

1178
01:44:22,720 --> 01:44:25,239
Take measure for them at least.

1179
01:44:37,480 --> 01:44:40,479
the Executioner of Roman Empire...

1180
01:44:42,520 --> 01:44:45,759
We're done here, Andra. Let's go.

1181
01:44:47,960 --> 01:44:51,559
Who is the Executioner of Roman Empire, Holofira?

1182
01:44:55,440 --> 01:44:58,239
Let's go, Andra! Come on;

1183
01:45:10,520 --> 01:45:12,519
Brother.

1184
01:45:12,680 --> 01:45:14,999
Where is Holofira going?

1185
01:45:15,320 --> 01:45:18,799
-Are you alright?
-It's a little complicated, brother.

1186
01:45:18,920 --> 01:45:22,039
Are you two affected by the evil eye?

1187
01:45:26,520 --> 01:45:28,919
It’s complicated.

1188
01:45:29,400 --> 01:45:31,559
But I will figure it out.

1189
01:45:32,640 --> 01:45:34,519
We will, brother.

1190
01:45:34,680 --> 01:45:37,359
What about you? Tell me.

1191
01:45:37,840 --> 01:45:40,399
I won’t let my heart speak anymore.

1192
01:45:40,760 --> 01:45:43,759
My only guide will be my mind.

1193
01:45:44,200 --> 01:45:47,039
It always shows me the right way.

1194
01:45:48,760 --> 01:45:50,679
Let’s go.

1195
01:45:54,200 --> 01:45:57,519
Well... I will tell Ulgen Hatun..

1196
01:45:57,640 --> 01:46:00,399
...to repel evil eyes from you!

1197
01:46:07,080 --> 01:46:09,559
Your duty will be harder.

1198
01:46:09,720 --> 01:46:13,199
You won't see your family and child.

1199
01:46:14,000 --> 01:46:17,039
You will be with Germiyans.

1200
01:46:17,760 --> 01:46:21,319
But I will be sure that they are safe.

1201
01:46:22,000 --> 01:46:24,639
Look after them, my Bey.

1202
01:46:50,040 --> 01:46:52,839
Osman brought Byzantine to their kneels.

1203
01:46:53,240 --> 01:46:56,279
He made all the lords obey him, father.

1204
01:46:57,760 --> 01:46:59,959
That hurts me, father.

1205
01:47:00,760 --> 01:47:04,559
I should have killed Osman
back then when I had a chance.

1206
01:47:04,640 --> 01:47:06,559
-None of these would...
-Shut up!

1207
01:47:06,640 --> 01:47:08,919
Mehmed.

1208
01:47:10,000 --> 01:47:12,879
Shut up.

1209
01:47:16,640 --> 01:47:18,759
We made a mistake.

1210
01:47:19,160 --> 01:47:23,799
And we will pay the price in silence.

1211
01:47:24,720 --> 01:47:27,759
Shut up.

1212
01:47:41,360 --> 01:47:46,319
Osman Bey, Lords sent the taxes you set for them.

1213
01:48:04,560 --> 01:48:06,519
Tell the lords..

1214
01:48:06,680 --> 01:48:10,799
If there is even one coin missing,

1215
01:48:11,480 --> 01:48:14,199
...they will feel my breath on their backs.

1216
01:48:30,520 --> 01:48:33,319
I couldn’t see that you were...

1217
01:48:33,520 --> 01:48:36,119
...on the right way.

1218
01:48:45,320 --> 01:48:47,919
The mistake making..

1219
01:48:48,160 --> 01:48:52,039
...a state collapse even
before it's established...

1220
01:48:52,600 --> 01:48:55,679
...is the desire of sultanate.

1221
01:48:57,920 --> 01:49:02,119
That’s what blinded your eyes, Yakup Bey.

1222
01:49:03,520 --> 01:49:07,799
But now I see that you
want to correct your mistake.

1223
01:49:08,960 --> 01:49:11,839
That makes you more valuable for me.

1224
01:49:12,160 --> 01:49:15,119
I want to give my blessings to
you in this world and in doomsday.

1225
01:49:17,320 --> 01:49:20,119
But there is still time.

1226
01:49:22,000 --> 01:49:25,359
What time are you talking about, Osman Bey?

1227
01:49:26,040 --> 01:49:28,119
The desire of sultanate..

1228
01:49:28,440 --> 01:49:31,559
...is like a fire growing
bigger from the ashes again.

1229
01:49:31,960 --> 01:49:34,839
Many couldn't keep their promises.

1230
01:49:38,040 --> 01:49:40,719
I want to see...

1231
01:49:41,160 --> 01:49:44,839
...if you'll have the same desire
when our state grows bigger.

1232
01:49:45,960 --> 01:49:49,639
I want to see if you'll stand behind me.

1233
01:49:50,880 --> 01:49:53,879
If you do,

1234
01:49:54,000 --> 01:49:56,879
...I will give my blessings to
you in this world and in doomsday.

1235
01:50:01,440 --> 01:50:02,959
But for now...

1236
01:50:06,640 --> 01:50:08,759
...I'm not giving my blessings to you.

1237
01:50:20,800 --> 01:50:23,239
Alright, Osman Bey.

1238
01:50:23,800 --> 01:50:26,279
Alright.

1239
01:50:26,960 --> 01:50:29,079
Alright.

1240
01:50:29,200 --> 01:50:32,799
Have a safe journey.
Take care.

1241
01:50:44,280 --> 01:50:45,439
Father.

1242
01:50:46,080 --> 01:50:49,239
-Don't do this.
-Shut up, Mehmed.

1243
01:50:49,360 --> 01:50:51,799
Get on your horse.

1244
01:51:38,640 --> 01:51:40,679
My Bey.

1245
01:51:41,040 --> 01:51:45,079
Holofira mentioned someone
to come to the frontiers.

1246
01:51:45,240 --> 01:51:48,879
-They call him the Executioner of Rome.
-Oh...

1247
01:51:51,120 --> 01:51:52,959
You say...

1248
01:51:53,160 --> 01:51:55,759
...things will get more complicated.

1249
01:51:56,240 --> 01:51:57,799
You know who he is, my Bey?

1250
01:51:57,880 --> 01:51:59,439
No.

1251
01:52:00,200 --> 01:52:03,359
But I heard about him.

1252
01:52:03,600 --> 01:52:05,479
They call him the Executioner.

1253
01:52:05,920 --> 01:52:10,239
He disguises and changes his name all the time.

1254
01:52:11,120 --> 01:52:14,399
In fact, he had rebelled against the emperor...

1255
01:52:14,720 --> 01:52:17,119
...and made his people get slaughtered.

1256
01:52:18,080 --> 01:52:20,639
It seems, he and the emperor made peace.

1257
01:52:20,880 --> 01:52:22,879
Now he will attack us.

1258
01:52:23,040 --> 01:52:26,519
My Bey, someone who did this to his own people...

1259
01:52:26,720 --> 01:52:29,399
...can do much more to his enemies.

1260
01:52:30,040 --> 01:52:32,759
Everything will be much harder.

1261
01:52:33,280 --> 01:52:35,159
May Allah help us.

1262
01:52:35,280 --> 01:52:36,719
Amen.

1263
01:52:36,960 --> 01:52:38,759
Let's go.

1264
01:53:04,480 --> 01:53:07,639
-Gonca Hatun!
-Ghazi.

1265
01:53:08,280 --> 01:53:10,359
Don't go!

1266
01:53:10,640 --> 01:53:13,119
-Ghazi.
-Mother, let me stop her!

1267
01:53:13,160 --> 01:53:15,119
Stop this!

1268
01:53:27,280 --> 01:53:29,599
Inglorious dastard!

1269
01:53:30,440 --> 01:53:34,079
Alps, you go on.

1270
01:53:37,120 --> 01:53:39,799
We’ll torture him until he speaks!

1271
01:53:40,840 --> 01:53:43,959
He'll tell where Gunduz Bey is before he dies!

1272
01:53:49,520 --> 01:53:51,839
Karacelasun or whoever you are.

1273
01:53:52,200 --> 01:53:54,919
We don't even know who is holding your leash.

1274
01:53:55,280 --> 01:53:59,799
What? Do you serve Tajeddin Noyan now?

1275
01:54:02,000 --> 01:54:03,439
What about vengeance?

1276
01:54:03,520 --> 01:54:07,319
I will kill you with my hands, Osman.

1277
01:54:08,000 --> 01:54:10,319
Whoever gives me this chance,

1278
01:54:10,400 --> 01:54:12,719
...I will serve him.

1279
01:54:13,520 --> 01:54:15,919
You tortured him well, it seems.

1280
01:54:16,160 --> 01:54:18,679
You did.

1281
01:54:20,760 --> 01:54:22,439
-Sami!
-My Bey.

1282
01:54:22,440 --> 01:54:26,039
-Start cutting him.
-As you order, my Bey.

1283
01:54:26,720 --> 01:54:29,679
Well... Leave the tongue.

1284
01:54:29,680 --> 01:54:31,159
As you order, my Bey.

1285
01:54:31,240 --> 01:54:34,319
He will speak with it.

1286
01:54:41,400 --> 01:54:43,759
Come on, man. Come on.

1287
01:54:44,040 --> 01:54:46,319
Come on.

1288
01:54:48,680 --> 01:54:52,399
Alright. I will tell you.

1289
01:54:52,560 --> 01:54:54,839
I will tell you what I know.

1290
01:55:22,040 --> 01:55:24,239
Great Olcaytu Khan’s nephew...

1291
01:55:24,320 --> 01:55:25,759
...Tajeddin Noyan...

1292
01:55:25,880 --> 01:55:28,319
...is coming to Yenisehir.

1293
01:55:30,840 --> 01:55:34,479
Let your Bey Osman know this.

1294
01:55:43,280 --> 01:55:45,039
Don’t be afraid, Osman's dog.

1295
01:55:46,480 --> 01:55:49,919
Alps, keep calm.

1296
01:55:50,760 --> 01:55:54,199
Tajeddin Noyan is coming
to this tribe-like city...

1297
01:55:54,400 --> 01:55:57,119
...only to talk.

1298
01:55:59,840 --> 01:56:02,199
Let him come.

1299
01:56:03,080 --> 01:56:06,639
-Inform Osman Bey.
-As you order, Baysungur Alp.

1300
01:56:12,920 --> 01:56:16,399
They transferred Elcim's father Gunduz Bey.

1301
01:56:16,960 --> 01:56:18,999
Where?

1302
01:56:19,120 --> 01:56:21,119
-Where?
-Speak!

1303
01:56:21,240 --> 01:56:23,759
To Tajeddin Noyan’s land.

1304
01:56:23,840 --> 01:56:26,319
To his headquarters.

1305
01:56:26,600 --> 01:56:28,599
It's near Karadere.

1306
01:56:31,200 --> 01:56:33,519
Can you go get him?

1307
01:56:34,960 --> 01:56:38,559
Will you go to the man who
you are hiding from with fear?

1308
01:56:39,800 --> 01:56:41,999
It's over, Osman.

1309
01:56:42,160 --> 01:56:45,679
Don’t care about Elcim’s
family but your own family!

1310
01:56:45,800 --> 01:56:47,919
Pull back the knife.

1311
01:57:05,320 --> 01:57:09,519
My Bey, Tajeddin Noyan is
coming to Yenisehir to talk.

1312
01:57:12,320 --> 01:57:15,639
What will you do now, Osman?

1313
01:57:18,720 --> 01:57:20,559
Look at me.

1314
01:57:20,640 --> 01:57:23,119
I didn’t kill you just because you spoke.

1315
01:57:23,320 --> 01:57:26,879
But I know what you did to Gunduz.

1316
01:57:28,240 --> 01:57:30,359
Alps.

1317
01:57:30,640 --> 01:57:33,439
He should only stand for me to take his head.

1318
01:57:33,880 --> 01:57:36,199
Break all the rest of himi

1319
01:57:36,880 --> 01:57:39,519
As you order, my Bey.

1320
01:57:46,360 --> 01:57:49,079
I don't think Saadet will behave.

1321
01:57:49,320 --> 01:57:52,359
Ulgen, keep your eyes wide open.

1322
01:57:53,640 --> 01:57:56,039
She must be furious now.

1323
01:57:56,200 --> 01:57:58,999
We should be cautious.

1324
01:58:01,160 --> 01:58:03,999
Ulgen, where is our guest?

1325
01:58:04,040 --> 01:58:07,119
She must be with Fatma. I prepared the meals.

1326
01:58:13,720 --> 01:58:15,479
Mother.

1327
01:58:15,800 --> 01:58:18,759
Meet Elcim Hatun.

1328
01:58:20,280 --> 01:58:23,279
kbasli Gunduz Bey's daughter.

1329
01:58:23,680 --> 01:58:26,799
Efendize Elcim Hatun.

1330
01:58:28,800 --> 01:58:30,439
Welcome, my daughter.

1331
01:58:30,640 --> 01:58:33,079
I am Malhun Hatun.

1332
01:58:33,280 --> 01:58:37,279
heard what happened to you. May it pass soon.

1333
01:58:41,320 --> 01:58:42,479
Bala Hatun.

1334
01:58:43,320 --> 01:58:46,319
We heard that you are from
Hayme mother’s lineage.

1335
01:58:46,400 --> 01:58:48,319
Welcome to our family.

1336
01:58:48,480 --> 01:58:50,479
Thank you.

1337
01:58:52,400 --> 01:58:55,439
When can I talk to Osman Bey?

1338
01:58:55,560 --> 01:58:57,719
My father, my aunt, my family...

1339
01:58:57,840 --> 01:59:00,599
...are waiting to be saved.

1340
01:59:05,040 --> 01:59:08,479
Osman Bey will call you when he has time.

1341
01:59:08,600 --> 01:59:10,439
You can have some rest if you want.

1342
01:59:10,480 --> 01:59:12,239
You can change your clothes and feel safe.

1343
01:59:12,320 --> 01:59:15,159
Ulgen. Let's prepare clothes for Elcim Hatun...

1344
01:59:15,280 --> 01:59:17,119
...and make her feel comfortable.

1345
01:59:17,320 --> 01:59:19,719
There is no need.

1346
01:59:21,720 --> 01:59:23,839
My tribe is entrusted to me...

1347
01:59:23,880 --> 01:59:25,839
...until my father sits on his chair.

1348
01:59:26,160 --> 01:59:30,079
And until then, I will wear these clothes.

1349
01:59:33,320 --> 01:59:35,239
I don't understand. Why?

1350
01:59:35,480 --> 01:59:39,719
To keep our people strong, Bala Hatun.

1351
01:59:40,280 --> 01:59:41,959
I have to dress like a man..

1352
01:59:42,200 --> 01:59:45,359
..until my father comes.

1353
01:59:50,160 --> 01:59:53,079
You thought well, Elcim Hatun.

1354
01:59:53,400 --> 01:59:57,599
People will feel strong
when they see you like this.

1355
01:59:57,760 --> 02:00:01,999
If Allah permits you will come
together with your father and aunt soon.

1356
02:00:02,160 --> 02:00:04,399
If Allah permits.

1357
02:00:05,960 --> 02:00:07,959
Can I come in?

1358
02:00:08,240 --> 02:00:10,959
Come in, Kismet.

1359
02:00:11,720 --> 02:00:15,079
Bala Hatun, Osman Bey is
waiting for you at the council.

1360
02:00:15,560 --> 02:00:18,639
Thanks to Allah.

1361
02:00:26,320 --> 02:00:29,079
She is very smart and brave.

1362
02:00:29,160 --> 02:00:31,679
Praise be!

1363
02:00:35,480 --> 02:00:38,319
You would not allow me
if I tried to dress like that...

1364
02:00:38,320 --> 02:00:41,759
...but you are speaking highly of
another mother's daughter; -Look at you...

1365
02:00:41,760 --> 02:00:46,519
My coy daughter is a little jealous these days.

1366
02:00:53,560 --> 02:00:55,159
Bala...

1367
02:00:56,320 --> 02:01:00,159
What do you think? I guess you did not like her.

1368
02:01:01,200 --> 02:01:04,599
Let's get to know her first, time will show us.

1369
02:01:05,160 --> 02:01:08,199
Come on, let's go.

1370
02:01:14,560 --> 02:01:18,559
I want Germiyan’s all honourable Commanders...

1371
02:01:18,640 --> 02:01:21,279
...to come to Kutahya, Kanyumaz.

1372
02:01:21,400 --> 02:01:23,999
Before the disaster named Tajeddin Noyan...

1373
02:01:24,120 --> 02:01:26,519
...surrounds these lands...

1374
02:01:26,600 --> 02:01:28,399
...we will take precautions.

1375
02:01:28,680 --> 02:01:30,439
Yes my Sultan.

1376
02:01:30,520 --> 02:01:32,439
The real disaster is at the border.

1377
02:01:32,720 --> 02:01:34,919
It is not the right time to go to Kutahya.

1378
02:01:35,080 --> 02:01:37,559
What are you trying to say, Mehmet?

1379
02:01:38,160 --> 02:01:39,999
Osman rebelled against you...

1380
02:01:40,240 --> 02:01:42,879
...his Sultan, and declared his sovereign Beylic.

1381
02:01:43,040 --> 02:01:46,679
It was not enough, he took
the Princess from llkhanate.

1382
02:01:46,720 --> 02:01:50,399
And he got over all the problems.

1383
02:01:50,760 --> 02:01:53,559
Now if he defeats Tajeddin Noyan..

1384
02:01:53,640 --> 02:01:56,079
...no one will be able to stop Osman.

1385
02:01:56,320 --> 02:02:00,319
Mehmeti I see and know...

1386
02:02:00,800 --> 02:02:02,639
...everything.

1387
02:02:02,680 --> 02:02:06,479
That is why I am going back to Kutahya.

1388
02:02:06,640 --> 02:02:11,759
If Osman defeats the disaster
named Tajeddin as well...

1389
02:02:12,080 --> 02:02:16,919
...one day, he might become our Sultan.

1390
02:02:18,280 --> 02:02:20,639
Do you think I'm too stupid...

1391
02:02:20,680 --> 02:02:23,399
...to see this?

1392
02:02:25,160 --> 02:02:30,879
Don’t forget. Your sword will be
your mind, and your shield will be...

1393
02:02:31,200 --> 02:02:34,759
..Osman's enemies.

1394
02:02:36,040 --> 02:02:39,159
We will not solve this issue with blood...

1395
02:02:39,280 --> 02:02:41,879
...but with wisdom.

1396
02:02:42,320 --> 02:02:45,959
Do you understand me now, Mehmet?

1397
02:02:46,720 --> 02:02:49,039
I do, father.

1398
02:02:50,400 --> 02:02:53,199
Gonca. Mehmet.

1399
02:02:53,480 --> 02:02:56,159
While I am in Kutahya..

1400
02:02:56,160 --> 02:02:59,199
...you will manage the frontiers' marketplace.

1401
02:02:59,600 --> 02:03:03,559
I will be informed about every step you take.

1402
02:03:03,640 --> 02:03:06,039
Yes, father.

1403
02:03:07,720 --> 02:03:12,079
Do not do anything without informing me.

1404
02:03:12,200 --> 02:03:14,719
Yes, father.

1405
02:03:35,320 --> 02:03:37,479
My Sultan...

1406
02:03:37,680 --> 02:03:40,519
I want to come with you.

1407
02:03:46,000 --> 02:03:50,439
I have no one left to go to other than you.

1408
02:03:51,920 --> 02:03:55,599
Ulgen left me.

1409
02:03:55,760 --> 02:03:58,719
My son turned away from me.

1410
02:04:01,800 --> 02:04:03,639
Cerkutay...

1411
02:04:03,760 --> 02:04:07,679
You didn’t tell Osman about me...

1412
02:04:08,120 --> 02:04:10,119
...they tortured you.

1413
02:04:12,120 --> 02:04:14,279
You could speak.

1414
02:04:14,440 --> 02:04:17,679
You did not use the mistakes
I made to make me feel small.

1415
02:04:18,600 --> 02:04:20,839
My son...

1416
02:04:21,000 --> 02:04:24,399
...tried to kill you.

1417
02:04:26,000 --> 02:04:28,559
But still, you did not speak.

1418
02:04:32,480 --> 02:04:35,799
Thank you Cerkutay.

1419
02:04:36,160 --> 02:04:40,199
My door is always open to you.

1420
02:04:46,080 --> 02:04:50,599
I will always be the guard
of that door, my Sultan.

1421
02:04:59,880 --> 02:05:03,119
I know, I know.

1422
02:05:03,240 --> 02:05:06,239
You will be at the frontiers’ marketplace...

1423
02:05:06,320 --> 02:05:08,039
...with Mehmet...

1424
02:05:08,440 --> 02:05:11,079
...while I am in Kutahya.

1425
02:05:11,360 --> 02:05:16,639
You will prevent Mehmet from making a mistake.

1426
02:05:19,160 --> 02:05:22,119
As you order, my Sultan.

1427
02:05:40,280 --> 02:05:43,399
The executioner of Byzantine on one hand..

1428
02:05:43,680 --> 02:05:48,799
..Tajeddin Noyan on the other.

1429
02:05:50,040 --> 02:05:52,839
A great war is at our door.

1430
02:05:54,640 --> 02:05:57,639
Elcim has told us the situation.

1431
02:06:00,440 --> 02:06:04,039
We gathered the union of Turks as well.

1432
02:06:04,120 --> 02:06:06,759
For now.

1433
02:06:07,320 --> 02:06:10,679
I can not say how the war will be now.

1434
02:06:10,840 --> 02:06:16,439
However, it is certain that
it will not look like any other.

1435
02:06:18,160 --> 02:06:21,479
The father of Elcim is in
the hands of Tajeddin Noyan.

1436
02:06:21,600 --> 02:06:23,519
She told us what happened.

1437
02:06:23,760 --> 02:06:28,599
From now on, it is our duty.

1438
02:06:28,720 --> 02:06:30,599
May you prosper, Osman Bey.

1439
02:06:30,680 --> 02:06:34,479
My father has nearly a thousand
alps that did not get caught.

1440
02:06:34,920 --> 02:06:37,239
If you allow me..

1441
02:06:38,760 --> 02:06:43,239
..I will call them all to the war.

1442
02:06:43,360 --> 02:06:45,559
Alright.

1443
02:06:45,640 --> 02:06:47,519
-Boran.
-My Bey.

1444
02:06:47,680 --> 02:06:49,519
Take the seal and give it to the clerk.

1445
02:06:50,040 --> 02:06:52,359
Sure, my Bey.

1446
02:06:56,800 --> 02:06:59,319
The bigger our numbers..

1447
02:06:59,560 --> 02:07:01,839
..the better.

1448
02:07:02,040 --> 02:07:07,399
Now, Tajeddin Noyan wants to talk to me.

1449
02:07:07,920 --> 02:07:10,919
It seems he wants to bargain.

1450
02:07:11,440 --> 02:07:15,479
He will want us to bow down,
my Bey. He will want the princess.

1451
02:07:15,840 --> 02:07:20,279
More than that, he will want Elcim Hatun.

1452
02:07:32,240 --> 02:07:34,199
Are we allowed, my Bey?

1453
02:07:34,320 --> 02:07:36,879
Come in.

1454
02:07:38,440 --> 02:07:41,999
Tajeddin Noyan is at the gates.

1455
02:07:46,800 --> 02:07:48,439
What will we do, Osman Bey?

1456
02:07:48,640 --> 02:07:51,399
He won’t get what he hoped for..

1457
02:07:51,480 --> 02:07:55,239
..but what I want.

1458
02:08:11,480 --> 02:08:13,159
My Shahzade.

1459
02:08:13,240 --> 02:08:16,119
Tajeddin Noyan's messenger sends word.

1460
02:08:16,200 --> 02:08:17,359
What is it?

1461
02:08:17,480 --> 02:08:20,999
They have the captive women..

1462
02:08:21,440 --> 02:08:22,999
..and children..

1463
02:08:23,160 --> 02:08:25,319
..from Elcim Hatun’s tribe.

1464
02:08:26,320 --> 02:08:29,079
If we attack..

1465
02:08:29,440 --> 02:08:31,999
..they will kill them with one strike.

1466
02:08:33,280 --> 02:08:34,959
What will you do, Alaeddin Bey?

1467
02:08:35,120 --> 02:08:37,479
Don’t fall to your anger, son.

1468
02:08:37,560 --> 02:08:40,559
Their intention is to drag us into war.

1469
02:08:41,560 --> 02:08:44,279
Will he not come to talk?

1470
02:08:45,480 --> 02:08:48,999
Let him come. There won't be an attack.

1471
02:08:49,600 --> 02:08:53,359
There will be nothing but Osman Bey's bidding.

1472
02:08:53,800 --> 02:08:55,959
As you command, my Shahzade.

1473
02:09:03,520 --> 02:09:06,519
Tacettin Noyan Headquarters

1474
02:09:28,080 --> 02:09:30,159
Obviously, Tacettin Noyan...

1475
02:09:30,240 --> 02:09:32,679
..arrived at Yenisehir with his nokers.

1476
02:09:33,240 --> 02:09:35,399
The rest is preparing here.

1477
02:09:35,520 --> 02:09:37,399
To attack.

1478
02:09:37,720 --> 02:09:40,159
However, we will attack them..

1479
02:09:40,640 --> 02:09:43,039
..before they do.

1480
02:09:43,800 --> 02:09:46,919
-Boran, is it with us?
-My Bey.

1481
02:09:47,080 --> 02:09:49,439
It is, my Bey.

1482
02:09:49,760 --> 02:09:52,039
Alright.

1483
02:09:53,440 --> 02:09:55,479
Come on now, make way to us.

1484
02:09:55,600 --> 02:09:56,919
Sıre, my Bey.

1485
02:09:57,240 --> 02:09:59,199
Come on.

1486
02:11:09,640 --> 02:11:12,559
We didn't think Osman Bey was this young.

1487
02:11:12,760 --> 02:11:15,839
Where is Osman?

1488
02:11:18,360 --> 02:11:20,919
I am Osman Bey's son, Alaeddin Bey.

1489
02:11:22,760 --> 02:11:25,279
It is my duty to welcome you.

1490
02:11:25,400 --> 02:11:28,479
Who are you to be equal to me?

1491
02:11:34,320 --> 02:11:37,799
You are the nephew of Olcayto..

1492
02:11:39,880 --> 02:11:41,919
..the Emir of Emirs..

1493
02:11:42,000 --> 02:11:44,199
..Tajeddin Noya

1494
02:11:46,360 --> 02:11:47,999
And I am..

1495
02:11:48,200 --> 02:11:50,839
..the owner of these lands..

1496
02:11:51,160 --> 02:11:53,439
..the pioneer of Turks..

1497
02:11:53,680 --> 02:11:56,599
..Alaeddin, son of Osman Bey.

1498
02:12:02,160 --> 02:12:05,959
If brother Aktemur was here..

1499
02:12:06,920 --> 02:12:09,439
..he would’ve welcomed you instead.

1500
02:12:15,720 --> 02:12:18,919
Our rank is equal.

1501
02:12:19,960 --> 02:12:25,039
First, tell us why you are here.

1502
02:12:25,280 --> 02:12:30,599
I am here because you did not obey
Ulu'l-Emr (superiors) Alaeddin Bey.

1503
02:12:31,000 --> 02:12:34,519
You declare your tribe by yourself..

1504
02:12:34,680 --> 02:12:37,279
..abduct the bride of llhanids..

1505
02:12:37,480 --> 02:12:39,879
..Princess Maria.

1506
02:12:39,960 --> 02:12:43,639
You kill Gorklu Khan..

1507
02:12:46,360 --> 02:12:52,199
..pray that I haven't destroyed this city.

1508
02:12:58,520 --> 02:13:01,199
You are talking about Ulu’l Emr, however..

1509
02:13:02,360 --> 02:13:04,719
..do you obey..

1510
02:13:04,800 --> 02:13:07,359
..and expect us to do so?

1511
02:13:09,360 --> 02:13:14,519
W do not do anything but the orders of Allah.

1512
02:13:15,680 --> 02:13:18,799
Shahzade.

1513
02:13:22,520 --> 02:13:27,319
We are the sword of Allah on earth.

1514
02:13:27,360 --> 02:13:31,239
You will pay for what you did.

1515
02:13:33,000 --> 02:13:36,119
I am Tajeddin Noyan.

1516
02:13:36,200 --> 02:13:39,039
I will be your calamity.

1517
02:13:45,480 --> 02:13:49,039
Come on.

1518
02:14:49,400 --> 02:14:51,839
Come on.

1519
02:16:01,760 --> 02:16:05,319
Prisoners' tent.
There, Osman Bey.

1520
02:16:12,400 --> 02:16:15,359
Do not worry, we won’t leave
before getting your father.

1521
02:16:15,480 --> 02:16:18,439
Come on.

1522
02:16:34,959 --> 02:16:35,839
Father?

1523
02:17:19,200 --> 02:17:22,558
Welcome, Osman Bey.

1524
02:17:29,840 --> 02:17:32,839
I was waiting for you.

1525
02:17:51,547 --> 02:18:04,627
Visit turkision.com for more!